---
import { withBase } from '../lib/links';
const memories = [
  { number:'01', tag:'Decisions', title:'Keep the why.', text:'Record the tradeoff behind an implementation, along with its source. Give the next agent more than the final diff.' },
  { number:'02', tag:'Conventions', title:'Keep the way.', text:'Save project rules, test commands, and repository patterns so each session starts with the same working knowledge.' },
  { number:'03', tag:'Handoffs', title:'Keep the next step.', text:'Leave a concise record of completed work, open questions, and the next action before a session ends.' },
];
---
<div class="mm-homepage">
  <aside class="mm-development not-content" aria-label="Project availability">
    <span class="mm-development-badge">Local preview</span>
    <p><strong>Memory you can run today.</strong> Durable writes, full-text recall, revision history, and a project-scoped MCP server are implemented on both main and AI_coded.</p>
    <a href={withBase('/memory/')}>How memory works ↗</a>
  </aside>
  <section class="mm-home-section not-content" aria-labelledby="keep-context">
    <div class="mm-section-heading"><div><p class="mm-label">Less rediscovery. More continuity.</p><h2 id="keep-context">The context worth keeping.</h2></div><p>Save concise, verified knowledge your agent can use again.</p></div>
    <div class="mm-paths">{memories.map(m => <article class="mm-path"><div class="mm-path-top"><span class="mm-path-number">{m.number}</span><span class="mm-label">{m.tag}</span></div><h3>{m.title}</h3><p>{m.text}</p></article>)}</div>
  </section>
  <section class="mm-home-section mm-try-section" id="try-it" aria-labelledby="try-it-title">
    <div class="mm-try-copy not-content"><p class="mm-label">A small start. A lasting memory.</p><h2 id="try-it-title">Save once.<br /><span>Recall next session.</span></h2><p>Build Mammoth, choose a project, and save your first decision. Connect the same local store to an MCP-capable coding agent.</p><ul><li>No account or hosted database</li><li>No model or embedding service required</li><li>The same memory through CLI and MCP</li></ul><a href={withBase('/intro/install/')}>Installation guide →</a></div>
    <div class="mm-quickstart"><slot /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="mm-home-section not-content" aria-labelledby="memory-loop">
    <div class="mm-section-heading"><div><p class="mm-label">One project. Many sessions.</p><h2 id="memory-loop">A simple memory loop.</h2></div><a href={withBase('/memory/workflow/')}>Read the agent workflow →</a></div>
    <ol class="mm-architecture"><li><span class="mm-role-icon" aria-hidden="true">↓</span><span class="mm-label">01 / Recall</span><h3>Start with context</h3><p>Search the project’s memory for the task at hand. Bound the response size to keep the context window useful.</p></li><li><span class="mm-role-icon" aria-hidden="true">◇</span><span class="mm-label">02 / Work</span><h3>Verify and build</h3><p>Use remembered decisions as background. Check the current code and sources before acting on an old assumption.</p></li><li><span class="mm-role-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="mm-label">03 / Remember</span><h3>Leave a clear handoff</h3><p>Commit useful context to disk. Revision checks prevent a second agent from silently replacing a newer entry.</p></li></ol>
    <div class="mm-deeper"><p>Local SQLite commits with a write-ahead log. Literal full-text search. No automatic capture.</p><a href={withBase('/memory/#durability-and-boundaries')}>Storage and limits →</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="mm-invitation not-content" aria-labelledby="connect-agent"><div><p class="mm-label">Your tools. A shared memory.</p><h2 id="connect-agent">Connect your coding agent.</h2><p>Five focused MCP tools to remember, recall, read, inspect history, and forget.<br />Choose one project per connection, with an optional read-only mode.</p></div><a class="mm-button mm-button-primary" href={withBase('/memory/mcp/')}>Set up MCP ↗</a></section>
  <footer class="mm-home-footer not-content"><span>Mammoth · Durable context memory for coding agents.</span><a href="https://github.com/ProjectOrcha/Mammoth">Explore the source ↗</a></footer>
</div>
